----- stdout -----
Raise vm.swappiness for zram swap  core.memory.swappiness

  Why       When swap lives in zram, a swapped-out page is compressed into RAM rather than written
            to disk, so swapping early frees more usable memory at almost no cost. This raises
            swappiness to the value zram setups use, and only when zram is the swap the kernel fills
            first.
  Gets      More usable memory under pressure, at almost no cost, on a zram system.

  Needs     your password, because it changes something outside your home
  Here      not applicable, swap is on disk, not zram; the default swappiness is right

  Undo      gameready rollback
